    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What katakana is used for",
     "texto": [
      "Katakana has the **same sounds** as hiragana, but with different signs, which are straighter and more angular.",
      "It is used for **words that come from other languages** (almost all from English), for foreign names —yours included— and for country names.",
      "Words are adapted to Japanese sounds: «taxi» becomes **タクシー** (takushī), «test» becomes **テスト** (tesuto)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
