    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The line for long vowels",
     "texto": [
      "In katakana, a long vowel is marked with a line: **ー**. ケーキ is «kēki» (cake) and スキー is «sukī» (ski).",
      "The small **ッ** works the same as in hiragana: it doubles the consonant. サッカー is «sakkā» (football).",
      "Be careful with two pairs that look very alike: **シ** (shi) and **ツ** (tsu); **ソ** (so) and **ン** (n). Look at which way the strokes point."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
